nce ned stark is  the warden of the north  he is responsible for delivering the  king's justice  in this region of westeros ned stark is  the head of the house that i believe  this story is centered around  so it's very important that we meet all  of its members very early on  in this series here is also when we meet  jon snow  arguably one of the most important  members of house stark  now although this is bran's chapter it  does give us some interesting details  about jon snow  who is only 14 years old at the  beginning of the  story so ned stark executes the deserter  from the night's watch with one single  stroke of his sword  as they are heading back to winterfell  rob and john have a discussion about the  man who was just executed  rob says the deserter died bravely  whereas  john says no this one was dead of fear  you could see it in his eyes then it  says john's eyes were a gray  so dark they seemed almost black but  there was little they did not see  remember this line about jon's eyes for  later i will mention it again  at the end of the chapter it also says  jon was slender  where rob was muscular dark where rob  was fair  graceful and quick where his  half-brother was strong and fast  then john and rob begin to erase their  horses back  and it mentions one other interesting  thing about jon that i want you to  remember for later  it says when they begin to race rob was  laughing  but john was silent and intent i believe  these details about jon are a direct  connection to his direwolf ghost  who he will find at the end of the  chapter i will explain what i mean once  we get there  now we get to one of my favorite moments  from the scene when bran  and his father discuss the execution  even if you haven't read the books i'm  sure you will remember this from the  show  this is when bran said the ned robb says  the man died bravely  but jon says he was afraid this makes  bran  think and ask can a man be brave even if  he's afraid  ned says that is the only time a man can  be brave  then ned says do you understand why i  did it  bran thinks it might be because the man  was a wildling and wildlings are known  for kidnapping women  and selling them to the others or the  white walkers  ned says the man was an oath breaker a  deserter from the night's watch  no man is more dangerous the deserter  knows his life is forfeit if he is taken  so he will not flinch from any crime no  matter how vile  however this is not why ned is asking  bran the question  he isn't asking why the man should die  but why ned has to be the one to see it  through  ned says our way is the old way if you  would take a man's life  you owe it to him to look into his eyes  and hear his final words  and if you cannot bear to do that then  perhaps the man does not deserve to die  a man who hides behind executioners soon  forgets what death is  i love how ned takes a moment to drop  some knowledge on his son  by making sure he understands why he had  to execute the man  brain will need to take that lesson with  him because one day he might have to do  the same thing  now although he does sometimes make  mistakes i think this does show that ned  stark is a good father overall  he appears to be an honest man who is  also lawful  who likes to carry out each and every  action with honor and integrity  but as the story begins to unfold we  will see that ned will have to make some  very hard decisions that go against his  own code  in order to save his loved ones we will  also begin to see that most of ned's  beliefs are in his children as well  in a story that is full of greed  corruption and backstabbings  the starks will become one of the  families we will look to  for some hope now let's move on to the  final scene of the chapter  as i said before this was the first  image that came to george rr martin  when he began writing a song of ice and  fire this is when they find the  direwolves in the late summer snows  as ned and bran are having their  discussion 